                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "For all the somberness the trailers promised, it unfortunately delivered most in sombering my expectations for the game in its entirety. The glitchiness of the game gives it an unfinished air that makes the player less confident in their ability to progress, further instigated by the irritating boils that pop up in every aspect of the game. Whatever promise the game has in its current state is moot, but perhaps with time and care the game may recover to a healthy state. But by that point, would starting the game over again even be worth it? Hard to say.\n\n+ Good ambiance and visual storytelling\n+ Core gameplay is fun, albeit repetitive\n\n- Feels unfinished; buggy/glitchy\n- Camera is too close and frustrating\n- A little too vague with its direction\n\nRead the full review at https://www.keengamer.com/article/20115_mechanism-review",
